<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaResource_Scrapfields.xml           Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-13
  ============================================================================

  V1 ROW 4, override 3 of 3 (the registration half).

  Defs/MapGeneration/JawaScrapfields.xml declares the GenStepDef
  Jawa_ScatterScrapfields. A GenStepDef on its own runs on NO map. A
  MapGeneratorDef has to list it, exactly as a TerrainDef needs a biome to ask
  for it. This file is that listing.

  ===========================================================================
  THE TARGET, READ FROM CORE
  ===========================================================================
  Core/Defs/MapGeneration/BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml:4-15

      <MapGeneratorDef ParentName="MapCommonBase" Name="Base_Player">
        <defName>Base_Player</defName>
        <genSteps>
          <li>RocksFromGrid</li>
          <li>ScatterShrines</li>
          <li>CaveHives</li>
          <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Royalty">AnimaTrees</li>
          ...
        </genSteps>
      </MapGeneratorDef>

  <genSteps> is a PLAIN LIST of GenStepDef names, so <li> is correct here.
  Read from the node, not assumed. The list inherits and appends to
  MapCommonBase's own genSteps (Core CommonMapGenerator.xml:18), which is why
  this def can carry only five entries and still generate a whole map.

  ===========================================================================
  SCOPE: Base_Player ONLY, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE
  ===========================================================================
  Base_Player is the generator for the map the colony settles on, so it is
  the map the v1 gate is actually checked against. The alternative was to
  patch the ABSTRACT MapCommonBase, which would put scrap on encounter maps,
  faction bases and quest maps too. That is broader, more visible, and more
  blast radius than a v1 thin row is allowed to spend. One extra Operation
  aimed at /Defs/MapGeneratorDef[@Name="MapCommonBase"]/genSteps widens it
  later if the owner wants the whole planet littered.

  ===========================================================================
  SAFETY
  ===========================================================================
  Conditional test xpath is IDENTICAL to the inner Add's xpath, so if Core
  ever renames the def or restructures the node this becomes a silent no op
  rather than a red error.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>Jawa_ScatterScrapfields</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
